{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Route deviation is established on this trip's own trace. gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 18.0 km against a booked optimal of 10.0 km: an excess of 8.0 km and 80%. POL-RD-01 requires both establishment tests to pass, and both do (excess greater than 20% of optimal, and greater than 0.8 km absolute). Under POL-RD-01 the trace figure governs the threshold test and trip_record.actual_distance_km may not be cited for it; the two happen to agree here at 18.0 km, but the finding rests on the GPS artifact.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09113", "EV-TRIP-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The computed deviation status is additionally MATERIAL: 80% of optimal exceeds the 50% material threshold in POL-RD-01 (the absolute 8.0 km limb is not additionally needed once the percentage limb fires). Materiality under POL-RD-01 is assessed on the excess REMAINING after adjustment, and even after the closure adjustment below the remaining excess of 4.4 km still exceeds both establishment tests against the adjusted optimal of 13.6 km. A material deviation also requires the driver_profile check in POL-RD-06.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09113", "EV-FARE-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The LTA closure advisory exonerates the driver only up to the POL-RD-03 cap, and the cap bites hard here. The advisory names the Pelton Canal Link eastbound connector, a segment the booked optimal route traverses, and its window 18:14-18:55 covers the whole trip, so the exoneration is engaged. The justified excess is the lesser of the measured 8.0 km or 1.30 x (shortest lawful alternative 12.0 km - booked optimal 10.0 km) + 1.00 km tolerance = 3.60 km. So 3.60 km is exonerated and the remaining 4.4 km of excess is not, and is refundable under POL-RD-02 computed against the closure-adjusted optimal of 13.6 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09113-01", "EV-GPS-09113", "EV-TRIP-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure[0].justified_excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver did not merely take the diversion the closure required. The advisory itself records the shortest lawful route between the booked endpoints as 12.0 km, while the vehicle covered 18.0 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff: 6.0 km further than the lawful alternative and 4.4 km further than even the capped exoneration allows. POL-RD-03 caps exoneration on ADDITIONAL distance for exactly this reason - a closure explanation cannot be stretched to cover any distance a driver chooses to run.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09113-01", "EV-GPS-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Running POL-RD-02 against the closure-adjusted optimal route gives the refund arithmetically. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 13.6 + 0.28 x 27.2) x surge 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier + 0.80 platform fee + 1.00 ERP on the optimal route = 23.416. Refund = charged_total 31.42 - 23.416 = 8.004, and the payable figure rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 is 8.05. The adjusted duration of 27.2 minutes is the booked 20.0 minutes scaled by 13.6/10.0, as POL-RD-03 requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09113", "EV-TRIP-09113", "EV-ADVIS-09113-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure[0].recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is neither de minimis nor a full-refund case, and the figure returns the whole of the sum the rider contests. 8.004 is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor, and it is 25.5% of charged_total, far below the 90% at which POL-RD-02 would escalate the remedy. The result is a partial refund of SGD 8.05 - which is exactly the SGD 8.05 amount_contested_sgd, so the rider is made whole on the sum in dispute.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure[0].refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 2.80 charged at the off-route 'Industrial loop exit' gantry is already comprehended in the 8.05 figure and I do not ask for it on top. The recomputed fare carries only the 1.00 gantry lying on the optimal route (Pelton lawful diversion entry, on_optimal_route true); the 2.80 line is off the optimal route and is therefore already excluded by the POL-RD-02 recomputation. Under POL-RD-09 such charges are itemised separately for transparency but must NEVER be added to the POL-RD-02 figure, and adding them would double-count the same money.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09113", "EV-GPS-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components.optimal_route_erp",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace on which this claim rests is unimpaired, so no corroboration requirement and no escalation is engaged. It carries 205 fixes at a 10-second sampling interval over 100.0% coverage, with zero gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds. None of POL-RD-07 limbs (a) to (c) fires, so excess is measured from the trace itself, the claim does not need an independent source under POL-RD-07(ii), and POL-RD-10(3) is not triggered.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's POL-RD-08 burden is discharged. trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip identifier TRP-09113 with a consistent timeline (trip started 18:20:00 against a first fix at 18:20:00), and the excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold is measured from the unimpaired trace. The rider's own claim history does not add the extra corroboration requirement at the end of POL-RD-08: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0, so that factor is simply not engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09113", "EV-GPS-09113", "EV-FARE-09113", "EV-RPROF-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver cannot shift the unexcused excess onto the rider as a rider-requested detour. The only rider message in the chat log is 'Understood, please take the lawful diversion'; it names no road or place and carries waypoint_hint null, so under POL-RD-04 the corroboration test is undecidable on the record, the clause is unavailable, and the case is decided on the remaining clauses. Even read at face value, that instruction authorised the LAWFUL diversion - which the advisory fixes at 12.0 km - not 18.0 km of driving.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09113", "EV-ADVIS-09113-01", "EV-GPS-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure[0].shortest_lawful_alternative_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-06 driver_profile check was run and returns no repeat pattern, and I state that frankly rather than assert one. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 across 610 completed trips in 90 days, so neither limb of the pattern test is met (3 or more flags; or a ratio of 0.05 or more with at least 40 trips). No FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) and no conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) follow, and the remedy remains the POL-RD-02 arithmetic of SGD 8.05.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No relocation clause applies, so the booked optimal of 10.0 km (as adjusted under POL-RD-03) is the correct baseline and no longer 'amended' route may be substituted for it. pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 is not triggered at all and the driver cannot manufacture a larger baseline out of an amendment that never happened.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
